interview. I just did a story on the acoba part.&nbsp;

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:35.160
Speaker 2: Okay. So I'm curious because every&nbsp;
time Joe Biden says something about Taiwan life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:40.020
if China invades, we're going to send troops.&nbsp;
But every time that happens, it always seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:45.540
that the White House always backs pedal and say,&nbsp;
oh, we don't know about that or, oh, we don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:49.260
stand by that. What do you think about that?
Speaker 1: I think it's typical posturing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:55.200
It's you you you say something, the president&nbsp;
says something, a little hawkish. And then when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.640
there's a request for a clarification, you sort&nbsp;
of walk back a little bit and say it's not our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.920
